{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/480104-little-help-with-infrastructure-and-aether-production","id":480104,"title":"Little Help with Infrastructure and Aether production","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-04-14T05:50:45-07:00","id":480104,"title":"Little Help with Infrastructure and Aether production","content":"Hello Everyone,<br /> <br /> I intend to run my first demon game this weekend, and I am trying to fill in some gaps on my ideas.<br /> <br /> Basically I want to know how much Aether should an Infrastructure produce - and although I know this is around Narrator's discretion, how much is too much and how much is too little?<br /> <br /> the infrastructure in question is as following:<br /> <br /> Just a few meters from the corner of a busy street, there is this VideoRental Shop (VHS and no DVDs...). No one ever comes in, and the owner (an angel, of course) opens it everyday at exactly 9:02 and closes at 7:08pm. Although no tape is ever rented everyday at 3h22pm a guy (angel or stigmatic, undecided) passes by and drop one black non-labelled tape on the quick-drop service.<br /> At night, 2:30am, the Angel watches the tape for the next 2:30 hours (watching the tapes is his mission). I gather that at this time Aether should start being produced, but, coming to my question, around how much?<br /> <br /> Thanks <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5690-mithrael","name":"Mithrael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5690_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-14T06:31:09-07:00","id":480149,"title":"","content":"It really depends, IMO, on your players and how many of them you have and if you think they'll want to Suborn the Infrastructure for their own ends, etc.<br /> <br /> Essentially, make it as useful/useless as you want it to be <i>to the player characters</i>.<br /> <br /> I like this idea for Infrastructure, too. Makes you wonder what's on the tape...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3855-gebbethine","name":"gebbethine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3855_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"233"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-14T08:17:26-07:00","id":480254,"title":"","content":"This is a nice bit of Infrastructure. I'd say 1-3 points of Aether, but where can it be harvested? By watching other tapes on the shelves? By eating the stale snacks by the counter? From the fizzing screen the angel watches? What's the linchpin?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Onyx Path Freelancer: Demon Storyteller's Guide, Dark Eras, Night Horrors: Enemy Action</i><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/825063-storyteller-s-guide-extra-material\" target=\"_blank\">Storyteller's Guide Extra Material</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/899423-after-the-fall-bonus-material\" target=\"_blank\">After the Fall: Bonus Material</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/452-eremite","name":"Eremite","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar452_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-14T09:56:29-07:00","id":480359,"title":"","content":"I do believe you can harvest 4 aether per turn while hooked in. Add in the fact of getting in unnoticed and hooking in may(is) be a risk. So I'd rather go with a maximum capacity, lets say 12 since it isn't all that big. The catch here is yes you can get a lot when you hook in that first time but it takes time to recharge (maybe one at the conclusion of watching the tape). So if demons keep tabs on infrastructure they can know where will have the best reward for the risk of the infrastructure they know and what if the levels are lower than they should be? That could tie into them trying to discover a demon they do not know anything about. <br /> <br /> If watching the TAPES are what the infrastructure is built around maybe the old VCR is the linchpin because it is not just the tape but the tape played on that vac, on that tv, the specific observer all occurring day after day after day. The more it occurs the more it reinforces itself or something.<br /> <br /> The last detail I'd share is remember that aether is 'waste heat'. Essence processed by the machine that it can no longer use and if it doesn't have caryatids designed to clean it or demons siphoning it away that waste heat will build up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-16T23:27:59-07:00","id":483226,"title":"","content":"Hey guys thanks for the answers <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr.F.I.X.</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/480104-little-help-with-infrastructure-and-aether-production?p=480359#post480359\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I <br /> <br /> If watching the TAPES are what the infrastructure is built around maybe the old VCR is the linchpin because it is not just the tape but the tape played on that vac, on that tv, the specific observer all occurring day after day after day. The more it occurs the more it reinforces itself or something.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed that is what I was thinking about using as linchpin <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />. Although I have a twist for it: the VCR, although from the 80's is connected to a top-of-the-art computer. The basement has some air-conditioning used to keep the temperature cool. My idea was that the aether would be collected from the AC unit on top of the building. I dont want them to have to go inside the store to collect it at this moment. So I was thinking that 10-12 total would be good, and perhaps 1 to 3 points generated a day.<br /> <br /> My idea for this infrastructure is that the tapes have in them the Dreams of 3 specific individuals which the God-Machine is currently analyzing (A workaholic who has recurring nightmares, a drug-dealer who is able to enter other persons dreams, and a teenage girl with prophetic dreams).<br /> <br /> I am giving my players (2) different options on how to get in touch with the plot: they can know the dreamers, they can find out the Rental Store, they might follow the guy who is dropping the tapes (he is a Cultist of the &quot;Dream Catchers&quot; - they can get high and are addicted to dreams given to them by an Angel &quot;Kolya&quot; once a week). They can find out about the cameras that are taping the individuals while they sleep and trace them back to where they are being made (CrowTech Ind. where Kolya is a Lab Researcher). <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5690-mithrael","name":"Mithrael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5690_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-16T23:39:15-07:00","id":483230,"title":"","content":"Glad to help. I like the direction you are going.<br /> <br /> Smart to make the aether collection be in an accessible place for players so they can grow to be curious but not forced to be. It also makes sense that waste heat would accumulate in a way that seems like it is exiting the infrastructure to me just because it makes sense from a design stand point especially since the machine can't not observe aether and has no value for it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}